      "evidence": "conflicting-candidate-integration-repair/design.md: \"No mergeability. The conflict signal stays `merge-tree` in `_prepare`. GitHub `mergeable` is not read.\" The proposal's \"What Changes\" says \"GitHub mergeability is not read.\" The test `test_conflict_outside_generated_files_needs_integration_repair` also mocks `merge-tree`, not `mergeable`.",
      "id": "mergeable-conflicting-signal-not-read",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "Requirement item 3 is phrased in terms of GitHub `mergeable=CONFLICTING`, but the delivered behavior never reads GitHub mergeability. It relies only on the queue's own `merge-tree` check in `_prepare`. The two signals can differ, for example when GitHub reports CONFLICTING while the local `merge-tree` is clean or only touches generated files. In that case the candidate still takes the derived-merge path and can stay in blocked-retryable if that path fails for environment reasons. The narrowing was an explicit coordinator decision, so this is advisory."
    }
